import LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ShimuraCurve.EllipticPointStabilizer
import LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ShimuraCurve.FiniteAdelicAlgebra

/-!
# Elliptic points on the geometric components of the Shimura curve `X_H`

Let `O` be an order of a quaternion algebra `B` over `ℚ` with a `ℚ`-algebra map `ι : B → M₂(ℝ)`, `μ`
a polarization of `O` and `H` a subgroup of the enhanced group `Aut_{±μ}(O) ⋉ Ô^×`. With the ring
`B̂ = B ⊗ 𝔸_f` of `LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ShimuraCurve.FiniteAdelicAlgebra`, the
homomorphism `f : Aut_{±μ}(O) ⋉ Ô^× → B̂^× / ℚ^×`, `(w, x) ↦ w x`, gives the group `K_H ⊆ B̂^×`, the
inverse image of `f(H)`, and the complex points of the Shimura curve `X_H` (LMFDB `shimcurve`) are
`X_H(ℂ) = B^×_+ \ (ℍ × B̂^×) / K_H` (`Subalgebra.ShimuraCurvePoints`). The point `[τ, b]` lies on
the geometric component `Γ_b \ ℍ`, for `Γ_b = B^×_+ ∩ b K_H b⁻¹`, and its stabilizer group is the
image of the stabilizer of `τ` in `Γ_b / ℚ^×`. An elliptic point (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`)
is a point with a nontrivial stabilizer group, which can be of order `2`, `3`, `4` or `6`.

This file proves that every stabilizer group has order `1`, `2`, `3`, `4` or `6`, on every geometric
component. The group `K_H` normalizes `Ô`, being generated by `ℚ^×`, `Ô^×` and elements of
`N_{B^×}(O)`, so `Γ_b` normalizes `O_b = B ∩ b Ô b⁻¹`, which is an order of `B`: if `n b` and
`n b⁻¹` lie in `Ô` for a positive integer `n`, then `n² O ⊆ O_b ⊆ n⁻² O`, by `B ∩ Ô = O`. Hence
`Γ_b` is a subgroup of the group `N_{B^×}(O_b)^+` of positive-norm elements of the normalizer of
`O_b`, and its stabilizer groups are subgroups of those of `N_{B^×}(O_b)^+ / ℚ^×`, which have order
`1`, `2`, `3`, `4` or `6` (`Subalgebra.natCard_shimuraStabilizer_mem`, ZK8's theorem, for the order
`O_b`, the polarization `0` and the whole enhanced group, for which ZF7's `Γ_H^+` is
`N_{B^×}(O_b)^+`).

The geometric component through the points `[τ, 1]` is the component `Γ_H^+ \ ℍ` of
`LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ShimuraCurve.EllipticPoint`: `Γ_1 = B^×_+ ∩ K_H` is `Γ_H^+`,
since `B ∩ Ô = O`, and the elliptic points of `X_H` on it are those of that file.

As in `LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ShimuraCurve.EllipticPoint`, `B` is any `ℚ`-algebra
(central simple of dimension `4` for the stabilizer theorems), `O` an order, `μ` any element, `H`
any subgroup and `ι` any `ℚ`-algebra map. The finiteness of the double coset space
`B^×_+ \ B̂^× / K_H`, that is, of the number of geometric components, for open subgroups `H`, is not
proved. The double coset space `B^× \ (ℋ^± × B̂^×) / K_H` of LMFDB `shimcurve` is in bijection
with `B^×_+ \ (ℍ × B̂^×) / K_H` because `B` has elements of negative norm
(`AlgHom.exists_det_lt_zero`), which exchange the two half-planes, while an element of `B^×` fixing
a point of `ℍ` has positive norm; the bijection itself, for `B` central simple of dimension `4`, is
`Subalgebra.shimuraCurvePointsEquivDoubleCoset`, in
`LeanBridge.ForMathlib.NumberTheory.ShimuraCurve.DoubleCosetLevelGroup`, with the model
`UpperLowerHalfPlane` of `ℋ^±`.

## Main definitions

* `Subalgebra.enhancedGroupToFiniteAdelic`: the homomorphism `f : Aut_{±μ}(O) ⋉ Ô^× → B̂^× / ℚ^×`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraLevelGroup` (LMFDB `shimcurve`): the group `K_H ⊆ B̂^×`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraAdelicGamma`: the group `Γ_b = B^×_+ ∩ b K_H b⁻¹ ⊆ B^×`.
* `Subalgebra.adelicOrder`: the order `O_b = B ∩ b Ô b⁻¹`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraAdelicGammaPlus`: `Γ_b` as a subgroup of `N_{B^×}(O_b)^+`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraAdelicStabilizer` (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`): the stabilizer group of
  the point `[τ, b]`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints` (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`): the elliptic points
  of the geometric component `Γ_b \ ℍ`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraPositiveUnits`: the group `B^×_+` of the elements of positive norm.
* `Subalgebra.ShimuraCurvePoints` (LMFDB `shimcurve`): the complex points
  `X_H(ℂ) = B^×_+ \ (ℍ × B̂^×) / K_H`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraCurveEllipticPoints` (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`): the elliptic points
  of `X_H`.

## Main results

* `AlgHom.exists_det_lt_zero`: a quaternion algebra `B` with a `ℚ`-algebra map `B → M₂(ℝ)` has
  elements of negative norm.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraLevelGroup_le_completedOrderNormalizer`: `K_H` normalizes `Ô`.
* `Subalgebra.isQuaternionOrder_adelicOrder`: `O_b` is an order of `B`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraAdelicGamma_le_unitsNormalizer`: `Γ_b` normalizes `O_b`.
* `Subalgebra.natCard_shimuraAdelicStabilizer_mem` (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`): every
  stabilizer group has order `1`, `2`, `3`, `4` or `6`.
* `Subalgebra.quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints_iff_natCard_mem` (LMFDB
  `shimcurve.elliptic_points`): the elliptic points of `Γ_b \ ℍ` are the points whose stabilizer
  group has order `2`, `3`, `4` or `6`.
* `Subalgebra.quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff`: being an elliptic point of `X_H` does
  not depend on the representative `(τ, b)`.
* `Subalgebra.quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints`: the
  elliptic points of `X_H` are those of its geometric components.
* `Subalgebra.quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff_natCard_mem` (LMFDB
  `shimcurve.elliptic_points`): the elliptic points of `X_H` are the points whose stabilizer group
  has order `2`, `3`, `4` or `6`.
* `Subalgebra.shimuraAdelicGamma_one`: `Γ_1 = B^×_+ ∩ K_H` is the group `Γ_H^+` of
  `Subalgebra.shimuraGammaPlus`.
* `Subalgebra.quotientMk_one_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff` (LMFDB
  `shimcurve.elliptic_points`): the elliptic points of `X_H` through the points `[τ, 1]` are the
  elliptic points `Subalgebra.shimuraEllipticPoints` of `Γ_H^+ \ ℍ`.
-/

open Algebra Matrix Module MulAction OreLocalization Submodule UpperHalfPlane

open scoped Pointwise

lemma natCast_mul_mul_mul_eq {R : Type*} [Semiring R] (m n : ℕ) (x y z : R) :
    ((m * n : ℕ) : R) * (x * y * z) = n * x * y * (m * z) := by
  simp only [← nsmul_eq_mul, smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, smul_smul]

namespace AlgHom

variable {B : Type*} [Ring B] [Algebra ℚ B] [IsCentral ℚ B] [IsSimpleRing B]

/-- **A quaternion algebra `B` over `ℚ` with a `ℚ`-algebra map `ι : B → M₂(ℝ)` has elements of
negative norm**, `det ι(β) < 0`: the images under `ι` of a `ℚ`-basis of `B` form an `ℝ`-basis of
`M₂(ℝ)` (`AlgHom.linearIndependent_real_comp_basis`), and the open set of the coefficient vectors
of the matrices of negative determinant, which contains that of `diag(1, -1)`, meets the dense set
of rational vectors. Such an element exchanges the upper and lower half-planes, which is what
identifies `B^×_+ \ (ℍ × B̂^×) / K_H` with `B^× \ (ℋ^± × B̂^×) / K_H`. -/
lemma exists_det_lt_zero (ι : B →ₐ[ℚ] Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) (hB : finrank ℚ B = 4) :
    ∃ β : B, (ι β).det < 0 := by
  have : Module.Finite ℚ B := Module.finite_of_finrank_pos (by omega)
  let e : Basis (Fin 4) ℚ B := finBasisOfFinrankEq ℚ B hB
  let bR : Basis (Fin 4) ℝ (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) :=
    basisOfLinearIndependentOfCardEqFinrank (ι.linearIndependent_real_comp_basis e)
      (by simp [finrank_matrix])
  let f : (Fin 4 → ℝ) → ℝ := fun r ↦ (∑ i, r i • ι (e i)).det
  have hf : Continuous f := by
    fun_prop
  have hmem : f (bR.repr (diagonal ![1, -1])) < 0 := by
    have h : ∑ i, bR.repr (diagonal ![1, -1]) i • ι (e i) = diagonal ![1, -1] := by
      simpa [bR] using bR.sum_repr (diagonal ![1, -1])
    simp [f, h]
  have hdense : DenseRange (Pi.map fun (_ : Fin 4) (q : ℚ) ↦ (q : ℝ)) :=
    DenseRange.piMap fun _ ↦ Rat.denseRange_cast
  rcases hdense.exists_mem_open (isOpen_lt hf continuous_const) ⟨_, hmem⟩ with ⟨q, hq⟩
  exact ⟨∑ i, q i • e i, by simpa [f, Rat.cast_smul_eq_qsmul] using hq⟩

end AlgHom

namespace Subalgebra

variable {B : Type*} [Ring B] [Algebra ℚ B] {O : Subalgebra ℤ B} (hO : O.IsQuaternionOrder) (μ : B)
  (H : Subgroup (O.EnhancedGroup μ)) (b : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ)
  (ι : B →ₐ[ℚ] Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ)

lemma commute_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_algebraMap (q : ℚ) (y : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra) :
    Commute (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (algebraMap ℚ B q)) y := by
  have hd : IsUnit (q.den : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra) := by
    rw [← map_natCast (numeratorRingHom (R := O.completedOrder) (S := O.completedOrderPosNat))]
    exact numerator_isUnit (O.natDenom q.den_ne_zero)
  have h : O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (algebraMap ℚ B q) = q.num * ↑hd.unit⁻¹ := by
    refine (Units.eq_mul_inv_iff_mul_eq hd.unit).mpr ?_
    rw [IsUnit.unit_spec, ← map_natCast (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO), ← map_mul,
      ← map_natCast (algebraMap ℚ B), ← map_mul, Rat.mul_den_eq_num, map_intCast, map_intCast]
  rw [h]
  exact (Int.cast_commute q.num y).mul_left (Commute.units_inv_left (Nat.cast_commute q.den y))

/-- The group `ℚ^×` of the rational scalars in `B̂^×`, which is central. -/
noncomputable def finiteAdelicRatUnits : Subgroup O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ :=
  (Units.map ((O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).comp (algebraMap ℚ B)).toMonoidHom).range

instance : (finiteAdelicRatUnits hO).Normal :=
  Subgroup.normal_of_le_center fun _ ⟨q, hq⟩ ↦ Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mpr fun v ↦ Units.ext <| by
    rw [← hq]
    exact (commute_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_algebraMap hO q v).eq.symm

lemma normalizerRatUnits_le_comap_finiteAdelicRatUnits : O.normalizerRatUnits ≤
    (finiteAdelicRatUnits hO).comap ((Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom).comp
      O.unitsNormalizer.subtype) := by
  rintro γ ⟨q, hq⟩
  exact ⟨q, Units.ext <| congrArg (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO) (congrArg Units.val hq)⟩

/-- The homomorphism `Aut_{±μ}(O) → B̂^× / ℚ^×` induced by the embedding `B → B̂`, where
`Aut_{±μ}(O) ⊆ N_{B^×}(O) / ℚ^×`. -/
noncomputable def autPmMuToFiniteAdelic :
    O.autPmMu μ →* O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ ⧸ finiteAdelicRatUnits hO :=
  (QuotientGroup.map _ _ _ (normalizerRatUnits_le_comap_finiteAdelicRatUnits hO)).comp
    (O.autPmMu μ).subtype

variable (γ : O.unitsNormalizer) (hγ : (γ : O.NormalizerModScalars) ∈ O.autPmMu μ)

lemma completedUnitsToUnits_completedUnitsAction (x : O.completedUnits) :
    O.completedUnitsToUnits (O.completedUnitsAction μ ⟨_, hγ⟩ x) =
      Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (γ : Bˣ) * O.completedUnitsToUnits x *
        (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (γ : Bˣ))⁻¹ := by
  refine Units.ext ?_
  rw [Units.val_mul, Units.eq_mul_inv_iff_mul_eq, Units.val_mul]
  exact O.oreDiv_mul_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra γ (O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder x) hO

lemma comp_completedUnitsAction (g : O.autPmMu μ) :
    ((QuotientGroup.mk' (finiteAdelicRatUnits hO)).comp O.completedUnitsToUnits).comp
      (O.completedUnitsAction μ g).toMonoidHom = (MulAut.conj (autPmMuToFiniteAdelic hO μ
      g)).toMonoidHom.comp ((QuotientGroup.mk' _).comp O.completedUnitsToUnits) := by
  rcases g with ⟨w, hw⟩
  rcases QuotientGroup.mk_surjective w with ⟨γ, rfl⟩
  exact MonoidHom.ext fun x ↦ congrArg QuotientGroup.mk
    (completedUnitsToUnits_completedUnitsAction hO μ γ hw x)

/-- The homomorphism **`f : Aut_{±μ}(O) ⋉ Ô^× → B̂^× / ℚ^×`**, `(w, x) ↦ w x`, through which the
enhanced group acts on `B̂^×` by right multiplication (the `f` of LMFDB `shimcurve.is_coarse`,
extended to `Ô^×`). -/
noncomputable def enhancedGroupToFiniteAdelic :
    O.EnhancedGroup μ →* O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ ⧸ finiteAdelicRatUnits hO :=
  SemidirectProduct.lift ((QuotientGroup.mk' _).comp O.completedUnitsToUnits)
    (autPmMuToFiniteAdelic hO μ) (comp_completedUnitsAction hO μ)

/-- The subgroup **`K_H ⊆ B̂^×`** of a subgroup `H` of the enhanced group `Aut_{±μ}(O) ⋉ Ô^×`: the
inverse image of `f(H) ⊆ B̂^× / ℚ^×`, so that the Shimura curve `X_H` has complex points
`B^× \ (ℋ^± × B̂^×) / K_H` (LMFDB `shimcurve`). It contains `ℚ^×`, so it is not compact: for an
open compact `H`, it is the product of `ℚ^×` and an open compact subgroup, which give the same
double cosets, `ℚ^× ⊆ B^×` being central and acting trivially on `ℋ^±`. -/
noncomputable def shimuraLevelGroup : Subgroup O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ :=
  (H.map (enhancedGroupToFiniteAdelic hO μ)).comap (QuotientGroup.mk' _)

lemma conj_mem_completedOrderSubalgebra {y : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra}
    (hy : y ∈ O.completedOrderSubalgebra) :
    O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (γ : Bˣ) * y * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO ↑(γ : Bˣ)⁻¹ ∈
      O.completedOrderSubalgebra := by
  rcases O.mem_completedOrderSubalgebra_iff.mp hy with ⟨c, rfl⟩
  rw [← O.oreDiv_mul_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra γ c hO, mul_assoc, ← map_mul, Units.mul_inv, map_one,
    mul_one]
  exact O.mem_completedOrderSubalgebra_iff.mpr ⟨_, rfl⟩

lemma map_mem_completedOrderNormalizer :
    Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (γ : Bˣ) ∈ O.completedOrderNormalizer :=
  O.mem_completedOrderNormalizer_of_forall (fun _ ↦ conj_mem_completedOrderSubalgebra hO γ)
    fun _ hy ↦ by simpa using conj_mem_completedOrderSubalgebra hO γ⁻¹ hy

lemma finiteAdelicRatUnits_le_completedOrderNormalizer :
    finiteAdelicRatUnits hO ≤ O.completedOrderNormalizer := by
  rintro _ ⟨q, rfl⟩ y
  have h : Commute (↑(Units.map ((O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).comp (algebraMap ℚ B)).toMonoidHom
      q) : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra) y :=
    commute_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_algebraMap hO q y
  rw [h.eq, Units.mul_inv_cancel_right]

/-- **The group `K_H` normalizes `Ô`**: it is generated by `ℚ^×`, `Ô^×` and elements of
`N_{B^×}(O)`. -/
lemma shimuraLevelGroup_le_completedOrderNormalizer :
    shimuraLevelGroup hO μ H ≤ O.completedOrderNormalizer := by
  rintro k ⟨⟨x, w, hw⟩, -, hxw⟩
  rcases QuotientGroup.mk_surjective w with ⟨γ, rfl⟩
  have h : enhancedGroupToFiniteAdelic hO μ ⟨x, ⟨_, hw⟩⟩ = QuotientGroup.mk
      (O.completedUnitsToUnits x * Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (γ : Bˣ)) :=
    rfl
  rw [h, QuotientGroup.mk'_apply, QuotientGroup.eq] at hxw
  rw [← mul_inv_cancel_left (O.completedUnitsToUnits x *
    Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (γ : Bˣ)) k]
  exact mul_mem (mul_mem (O.completedUnitsToUnits_mem_completedOrderNormalizer x)
    (map_mem_completedOrderNormalizer hO γ)) <|
    finiteAdelicRatUnits_le_completedOrderNormalizer hO hxw

/-- The group **`Γ_b = B^×_+ ∩ b K_H b⁻¹`** of the geometric component `Γ_b \ ℍ` of the Shimura
curve `X_H` through the points `[τ, b]`, `τ ∈ ℍ`, for `b ∈ B̂^×`: the elements of `B^×` whose image
in `B̂^×` lies in `b K_H b⁻¹` and of positive norm, that is, with `det ι(γ) > 0`. -/
noncomputable def shimuraAdelicGamma : Subgroup Bˣ :=
  (shimuraLevelGroup hO μ H).comap ((MulAut.conj b⁻¹).toMonoidHom.comp
    (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom)) ⊓
    (GLPos (Fin 2) ℝ).comap (Units.map ι.toMonoidHom)

/-- The order **`O_b = B ∩ b Ô b⁻¹`** of `B`, for `b ∈ B̂^×`: the elements `x` of `B` such that
`b⁻¹ x b ∈ Ô`. Its normalizer contains `Γ_b`. -/
noncomputable def adelicOrder : Subalgebra ℤ B where
  carrier := {x | ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO x * ↑b ∈ O.completedOrderSubalgebra}
  mul_mem' {x y} hx hy := by
    have h : ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (x * y) * ↑b = ↑b⁻¹ *
        O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO x * ↑b * (↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO y * ↑b) := by
      simp [mul_assoc]
    rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, h]
    exact mul_mem hx hy
  add_mem' {x y} hx hy := by
    have h : ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (x + y) * ↑b = ↑b⁻¹ *
        O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO x * ↑b + ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO y * ↑b := by
      rw [map_add, OreLocalization.left_distrib, OreLocalization.right_distrib]
    rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, h]
    exact add_mem hx hy
  algebraMap_mem' n := by
    have h : ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (algebraMap ℤ B n) * ↑b = n := by
      rw [eq_intCast (algebraMap ℤ B), map_intCast, ← (Int.cast_commute n _).eq, mul_assoc,
        Units.inv_mul, mul_one]
    rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, h]
    exact O.mem_completedOrderSubalgebra_iff.mpr
      ⟨n, map_intCast (numeratorRingHom (R := O.completedOrder) (S := O.completedOrderPosNat)) n⟩

lemma mem_adelicOrder {x : B} :
    x ∈ adelicOrder hO b ↔ ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO x * ↑b ∈ O.completedOrderSubalgebra :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **`O_b = B ∩ b Ô b⁻¹` is an order of `B`**: if `n b` and `n b⁻¹` lie in `Ô`, then
`n² O ⊆ O_b ⊆ n⁻² O`, using `B ∩ Ô = O`, so `O_b` is a `ℤ`-lattice spanning `B`. -/
lemma isQuaternionOrder_adelicOrder : (adelicOrder hO b).IsQuaternionOrder := by
  rcases O.exists_natCast_mul_mem_completedOrderSubalgebra (b : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra) with
    ⟨n₁, hn₁, h₁⟩
  rcases O.exists_natCast_mul_mem_completedOrderSubalgebra (↑b⁻¹ : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra) with
    ⟨n₂, hn₂, h₂⟩
  have : Submodule.IsLattice ℚ (toSubmodule O) := hO
  let a : ℚˣ := Units.mk0 ((n₁ * n₂ : ℕ) : ℚ) (Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr (mul_ne_zero hn₁ hn₂))
  have hsmul (x : B) : a • x = ((n₁ * n₂ : ℕ) : B) * x := by
    rw [Units.smul_def, Units.val_mk0, Algebra.smul_def, map_natCast]
  have hlow : a • toSubmodule O ≤ toSubmodule (adelicOrder hO b) := by
    intro m hm
    rcases (Submodule.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists _ _ _).mp hm with ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    have e : ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (((n₁ * n₂ : ℕ) : B) * y) * ↑b =
        ↑n₂ * ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO y * (↑n₁ * ↑b) := by
      rw [map_mul, map_natCast, ← (Nat.cast_commute (n₁ * n₂) (↑b⁻¹ :
        O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra)).left_comm, mul_assoc, natCast_mul_mul_mul_eq]
    refine (mem_adelicOrder hO b).mpr ?_
    rw [hsmul, e]
    exact mul_mem (mul_mem h₂ (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_mem hO hy)) h₁
  have hup : toSubmodule (adelicOrder hO b) ≤ a⁻¹ • toSubmodule O := by
    intro x hx
    refine (Submodule.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists _ _ _).mpr ⟨a • x, ?_, inv_smul_smul a x⟩
    rw [hsmul]
    refine O.mem_of_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_mem hO ?_
    have e : O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (((n₁ * n₂ : ℕ) : B) * x) =
        ↑n₁ * ↑b * (↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO x * ↑b) * (↑n₂ * ↑b⁻¹) := by
      rw [← natCast_mul_mul_mul_eq, mul_comm n₂ n₁, map_mul, map_natCast]
      simp [mul_assoc]
    rw [e]
    exact mul_mem (mul_mem h₁ hx) h₂
  have hfg : (toSubmodule (adelicOrder hO b)).FG := by
    have : IsNoetherian ℤ (toSubmodule (adelicOrder hO b)) := isNoetherian_of_le hup
    exact Finite.iff_fg.mp inferInstance
  exact IsLattice.of_le_of_isLattice_of_fg ℚ hlow hfg

/-- **`Γ_b` normalizes the order `O_b = B ∩ b Ô b⁻¹`**, since `K_H` normalizes `Ô`. -/
lemma shimuraAdelicGamma_le_unitsNormalizer :
    shimuraAdelicGamma hO μ H b ι ≤ (adelicOrder hO b).unitsNormalizer := by
  intro γ hγ x
  have hk : ((MulAut.conj b⁻¹).toMonoidHom.comp (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra
      hO).toMonoidHom)) γ ∈ O.completedOrderNormalizer :=
    shimuraLevelGroup_le_completedOrderNormalizer hO μ H (Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hγ).1
  rw [mem_adelicOrder, mem_adelicOrder, hk]
  have e : ↑(((MulAut.conj b⁻¹).toMonoidHom.comp (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra
      hO).toMonoidHom)) γ) * (↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO x * ↑b) *
      ↑(((MulAut.conj b⁻¹).toMonoidHom.comp (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra
      hO).toMonoidHom)) γ)⁻¹ = ↑b⁻¹ * O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO (↑γ * x * ↑γ⁻¹) * ↑b := by
    simp [mul_assoc]
  rw [e]

lemma mem_shimuraGammaPlus_zero_top {O' : Subalgebra ℤ B} {δ : O'.unitsNormalizer}
    (hδ : 0 < (O'.normalizerToGL ι δ).val.det) : δ ∈ O'.shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι := by
  refine Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨⟨SemidirectProduct.inr ⟨_, δ, Or.inl (by simp), rfl⟩, trivial, ?_⟩,
    (mem_glpos _).mpr hδ⟩
  rw [autPmMuMul, SemidirectProduct.lift_inr]
  rfl

/-- The group **`Γ_b = B^×_+ ∩ b K_H b⁻¹`** of the component `Γ_b \ ℍ` of `X_H`, as a subgroup of
the group `N_{B^×}(O_b)^+` of the elements of positive norm of the normalizer of the order
`O_b = B ∩ b Ô b⁻¹`, which contains it (`Subalgebra.shimuraAdelicGamma_le_unitsNormalizer`); the
latter is ZF7's `Γ_H^+` for `O_b`, the polarization `0` and the whole enhanced group. -/
noncomputable def shimuraAdelicGammaPlus : Subgroup ((adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι) :=
  (shimuraAdelicGamma hO μ H b ι).comap ((adelicOrder hO b).unitsNormalizer.subtype.comp
    ((adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι).subtype)

variable (τ : ℍ)

/-- The **stabilizer group** (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`) of the point `[τ, b]` of the
Shimura curve `X_H`, on its geometric component `Γ_b \ ℍ`: the image of the stabilizer of `τ` in
`Γ_b` in the group `N_{B^×}(O_b)^+ / ℚ^×` acting on `ℍ`, isomorphic to `Stab_{Γ_b}(τ) / ℚ^×`. -/
noncomputable def shimuraAdelicStabilizer : Subgroup ((adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι ⧸
    (adelicOrder hO b).normalizerRatUnits.subgroupOf ((adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι)) :=
  (stabilizer ((adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι) τ ⊓
    shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι).map (QuotientGroup.mk' _)

lemma shimuraAdelicStabilizer_le :
    shimuraAdelicStabilizer hO μ H b ι τ ≤ (adelicOrder hO b).shimuraStabilizer 0 ⊤ ι τ := by
  rw [shimuraAdelicStabilizer, shimuraStabilizer_eq_map]
  exact Subgroup.map_mono inf_le_left

lemma mem_one_two_three_four_six_of_dvd {d c : ℕ} (h : d ∣ c)
    (hc : c ∈ ({1, 2, 3, 4, 6} : Finset ℕ)) : d ∈ ({1, 2, 3, 4, 6} : Finset ℕ) := by
  simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hc ⊢
  rcases hc with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl <;>
  · have hd : d ≤ 6 := (Nat.le_of_dvd (by norm_num) h).trans (by norm_num)
    interval_cases d <;> omega

variable [IsCentral ℚ B] [IsSimpleRing B] in
/-- **The stabilizer group of a point of the Shimura curve `X_H` has order `1`, `2`, `3`, `4` or
`6`** (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`), on every geometric component `Γ_b \ ℍ`, for an order `O`
of a quaternion algebra `B` over `ℚ`: it is a subgroup of the stabilizer group of `τ` for the order
`O_b`, of order `1`, `2`, `3`, `4` or `6` (`Subalgebra.natCard_shimuraStabilizer_mem`). -/
lemma natCard_shimuraAdelicStabilizer_mem (hB : finrank ℚ B = 4) :
    Nat.card (shimuraAdelicStabilizer hO μ H b ι τ) ∈ ({1, 2, 3, 4, 6} : Finset ℕ) :=
  mem_one_two_three_four_six_of_dvd (Subgroup.card_dvd_of_le (shimuraAdelicStabilizer_le hO μ H b ι
    τ)) (natCard_shimuraStabilizer_mem hB (isQuaternionOrder_adelicOrder hO b))

/-- The **elliptic points** (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`) of the geometric component
`Γ_b \ ℍ` of the Shimura curve `X_H`, for `b ∈ B̂^×`: the orbits of the points `τ` of `ℍ` fixed by
an element of `Γ_b` which is not a rational scalar, that is, with nontrivial stabilizer group. -/
noncomputable def shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints :
    Set (orbitRel.Quotient (shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι) ℍ) :=
  Quotient.mk _ '' {τ | ∃ γ : shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι, γ • τ = τ ∧
    (((γ : (adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι) : (adelicOrder hO b).unitsNormalizer) ∉
      (adelicOrder hO b).normalizerRatUnits)}

lemma quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints_iff :
    (Quotient.mk _ τ : orbitRel.Quotient (shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι) ℍ) ∈
    shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints hO μ H b ι ↔ ∃ γ : shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι, γ • τ = τ ∧
    (((γ : (adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι) : (adelicOrder hO b).unitsNormalizer) ∉
      (adelicOrder hO b).normalizerRatUnits) := by
  refine ⟨?_, fun h ↦ ⟨τ, h, rfl⟩⟩
  rintro ⟨τ', ⟨γ, hγ, hγN⟩, h⟩
  rcases Quotient.exact h with ⟨δ, hδ⟩
  have hδ' : δ • τ = τ' := hδ
  refine ⟨δ⁻¹ * γ * δ, ?_, fun hN ↦ hγN ?_⟩
  · rw [mul_smul, mul_smul, hδ', hγ, ← hδ', inv_smul_smul]
  · simpa [mul_assoc] using
      (inferInstance : (adelicOrder hO b).normalizerRatUnits.Normal).conj_mem _ hN δ

lemma shimuraAdelicStabilizer_ne_bot_iff : shimuraAdelicStabilizer hO μ H b ι τ ≠ ⊥ ↔
    ∃ γ : shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι, γ • τ = τ ∧
    (((γ : (adelicOrder hO b).shimuraGammaPlus 0 ⊤ ι) : (adelicOrder hO b).unitsNormalizer) ∉
      (adelicOrder hO b).normalizerRatUnits) := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun ⟨γ, hγτ, hγN⟩ ↦ Subgroup.ne_bot_iff_exists_ne_one.mpr
    ⟨⟨QuotientGroup.mk' _ γ, γ, ⟨hγτ, γ.2⟩, rfl⟩, fun h ↦ hγN ?_⟩⟩
  · rcases Subgroup.ne_bot_iff_exists_ne_one.mp h with ⟨⟨_, γ, ⟨hγτ, hγ⟩, rfl⟩, hne⟩
    exact ⟨⟨γ, hγ⟩, hγτ, fun hN ↦ hne <| Subtype.ext <|
      (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff γ).mpr (Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mpr hN)⟩
  · exact Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mp ((QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).mp (congrArg Subtype.val h))

variable [IsCentral ℚ B] [IsSimpleRing B] in
/-- **The elliptic points of every geometric component `Γ_b \ ℍ` of the Shimura curve `X_H` are the
points whose stabilizer group has order `2`, `3`, `4` or `6`** (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`),
for an order `O` of a quaternion algebra `B` over `ℚ`. -/
lemma quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints_iff_natCard_mem (hB : finrank ℚ B = 4) :
    (Quotient.mk _ τ : orbitRel.Quotient (shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι) ℍ) ∈
    shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints hO μ H b ι ↔
    Nat.card (shimuraAdelicStabilizer hO μ H b ι τ) ∈ ({2, 3, 4, 6} : Finset ℕ) := by
  have h : Nat.card (shimuraAdelicStabilizer hO μ H b ι τ) ∈ ({1, 2, 3, 4, 6} : Finset ℕ) :=
    natCard_shimuraAdelicStabilizer_mem hO μ H b ι τ hB
  rw [quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints_iff, ← shimuraAdelicStabilizer_ne_bot_iff, Ne,
    ← Subgroup.card_eq_one]
  simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at h ⊢
  omega

/-- The group **`B^×_+`** of the elements of positive norm of `B^×`, those `γ` with
`det ι(γ) > 0`. -/
noncomputable def shimuraPositiveUnits : Subgroup Bˣ :=
  (GLPos (Fin 2) ℝ).comap (Units.map ι.toMonoidHom)

noncomputable instance :
    SMul (shimuraPositiveUnits ι × shimuraLevelGroup hO μ H) (ℍ × O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ) where
  smul g p := (Units.map ι.toMonoidHom g.1 • p.1,
    Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom g.1 * p.2 *
      (g.2 : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ)⁻¹)

lemma shimuraPositiveUnits_prod_smul_def (g : shimuraPositiveUnits ι × shimuraLevelGroup hO μ H)
    (p : ℍ × O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ) : g • p = (Units.map ι.toMonoidHom g.1 • p.1,
    Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom g.1 * p.2 *
      (g.2 : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ)⁻¹) :=
  rfl

noncomputable instance :
    MulAction (shimuraPositiveUnits ι × shimuraLevelGroup hO μ H) (ℍ × O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ) where
  one_smul p := by
    rw [shimuraPositiveUnits_prod_smul_def]
    refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;> simp
  mul_smul g h p := by
    rw [shimuraPositiveUnits_prod_smul_def, shimuraPositiveUnits_prod_smul_def,
      shimuraPositiveUnits_prod_smul_def]
    refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;> simp [mul_smul, mul_assoc]

/-- The **complex points `X_H(ℂ) = B^×_+ \ (ℍ × B̂^×) / K_H`** (LMFDB `shimcurve`) of the Shimura
curve `X_H`, the orbits of `B^×_+ × K_H` acting on `ℍ × B̂^×` by
`(β, k) • (τ, b) = (β τ, β b k⁻¹)`. Since `B^×` contains elements of negative norm
(`AlgHom.exists_det_lt_zero`), which exchange the two half-planes, this is the double coset space
`B^× \ (ℋ^± × B̂^×) / K_H` of LMFDB `shimcurve`, with stabilizer groups of the same order
(`Subalgebra.shimuraCurvePointsEquivDoubleCoset`,
`Subalgebra.natCard_shimuraDoubleCosetStabilizer_ofUpperHalfPlane`, for `B` central simple of
dimension `4`). Its geometric components are the `Γ_b \ ℍ`, for `b` in the double cosets
`B^×_+ \ B̂^× / K_H`. -/
abbrev ShimuraCurvePoints : Type _ :=
  orbitRel.Quotient (shimuraPositiveUnits ι × shimuraLevelGroup hO μ H) (ℍ × O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ)

/-- The **elliptic points** (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`) of the Shimura curve `X_H`: the
points `[τ, b]` of `X_H(ℂ)` with nontrivial stabilizer group, that is, such that `τ` is fixed by an
element of `Γ_b = B^×_+ ∩ b K_H b⁻¹` which is not a rational scalar, the union of the elliptic
points of the geometric components `Γ_b \ ℍ`. -/
noncomputable def shimuraCurveEllipticPoints : Set (ShimuraCurvePoints hO μ H ι) :=
  Quotient.mk _ '' {p | ∃ γ ∈ shimuraAdelicGamma hO μ H p.2 ι,
    Units.map ι.toMonoidHom γ • p.1 = p.1 ∧ γ ∉ (Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B)).range}

/-- **Being an elliptic point of `X_H` is a property of the point**: `[τ, b]` is an elliptic point
exactly when some element of `Γ_b` other than a rational scalar fixes `τ`, the groups `Γ_b` and the
stabilizers of the representatives of a point being conjugate. -/
lemma quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff :
    (Quotient.mk _ (τ, b) : ShimuraCurvePoints hO μ H ι) ∈ shimuraCurveEllipticPoints hO μ H ι ↔
    ∃ γ ∈ shimuraAdelicGamma hO μ H b ι, Units.map ι.toMonoidHom γ • τ = τ ∧
      γ ∉ (Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B)).range := by
  refine ⟨?_, fun h ↦ ⟨(τ, b), h, rfl⟩⟩
  rintro ⟨⟨τ', b'⟩, ⟨γ, hγ, hγτ, hγQ⟩, h⟩
  rcases Quotient.exact h with ⟨⟨β, k⟩, hβk⟩
  have h₁ : Units.map ι.toMonoidHom β • τ = τ' :=
    congrArg Prod.fst hβk
  have h₂ : Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom β * b *
      (k : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ)⁻¹ = b' :=
    congrArg Prod.snd hβk
  refine ⟨(β : Bˣ)⁻¹ * γ * β, Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨?_, mul_mem (mul_mem (inv_mem β.2)
    (Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hγ).2) β.2⟩, ?_, fun hQ ↦ hγQ ?_⟩
  · have e : ((MulAut.conj b⁻¹).toMonoidHom.comp (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra
        hO).toMonoidHom)) ((β : Bˣ)⁻¹ * γ * β) = (k : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ)⁻¹ *
        ((MulAut.conj b'⁻¹).toMonoidHom.comp (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom)
        γ) * k := by
      rw [← h₂]
      simp only [MonoidHom.comp_apply, MulEquiv.coe_toMonoidHom, MulAut.conj_apply]
      simp only [map_mul, map_inv]
      group
    rw [Subgroup.mem_comap, e]
    exact mul_mem (mul_mem (inv_mem k.2) (Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hγ).1) k.2
  · rw [map_mul, map_mul, mul_smul, mul_smul, h₁, hγτ, ← h₁, map_inv, inv_smul_smul]
  · rcases hQ with ⟨q, hq⟩
    refine ⟨q, ?_⟩
    have hc : Commute (Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B) q) (β : Bˣ) :=
      Units.ext <| Algebra.commutes (q : ℚ) _
    have e : γ = β * ((β : Bˣ)⁻¹ * γ * β) * (β : Bˣ)⁻¹ := by
      group
    rw [e, ← hq, ← hc.eq, mul_inv_cancel_right]

lemma exists_iff_quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints :
    (∃ γ ∈ shimuraAdelicGamma hO μ H b ι, Units.map ι.toMonoidHom γ • τ = τ ∧
      γ ∉ (Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B)).range) ↔
    (Quotient.mk _ τ : orbitRel.Quotient (shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι) ℍ) ∈
      shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints hO μ H b ι := by
  rw [quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints_iff]
  refine ⟨fun ⟨γ, hγ, hγτ, hγQ⟩ ↦ ⟨⟨⟨⟨γ, shimuraAdelicGamma_le_unitsNormalizer hO μ H b ι hγ⟩,
    mem_shimuraGammaPlus_zero_top ι ((mem_glpos _).mp (Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hγ).2)⟩, hγ⟩, hγτ,
    fun h ↦ hγQ (Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mp h)⟩, fun ⟨δ, hδτ, hδQ⟩ ↦ ⟨_, δ.2, hδτ,
    fun h ↦ hδQ (Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mpr h)⟩⟩

/-- **The elliptic points of `X_H` are those of its geometric components**: `[τ, b]` is an
elliptic point of `X_H` exactly when the orbit of `τ` is an elliptic point of `Γ_b \ ℍ`. -/
lemma quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints :
    (Quotient.mk _ (τ, b) : ShimuraCurvePoints hO μ H ι) ∈ shimuraCurveEllipticPoints hO μ H ι ↔
    (Quotient.mk _ τ : orbitRel.Quotient (shimuraAdelicGammaPlus hO μ H b ι) ℍ) ∈
      shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints hO μ H b ι :=
  (quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff hO μ H b ι τ).trans
    (exists_iff_quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints hO μ H b ι τ)

variable [IsCentral ℚ B] [IsSimpleRing B] in
/-- **The elliptic points of the Shimura curve `X_H` are the points whose stabilizer group has order
`2`, `3`, `4` or `6`** (LMFDB `shimcurve.elliptic_points`), for an order `O` of a quaternion
algebra `B` over `ℚ`: the stabilizer group of every point `[τ, b]` has order `1`, `2`, `3`, `4` or
`6` (`Subalgebra.natCard_shimuraAdelicStabilizer_mem`), and the point is elliptic exactly when it
is not `1`. -/
lemma quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff_natCard_mem (hB : finrank ℚ B = 4) :
    (Quotient.mk _ (τ, b) : ShimuraCurvePoints hO μ H ι) ∈ shimuraCurveEllipticPoints hO μ H ι ↔
    Nat.card (shimuraAdelicStabilizer hO μ H b ι τ) ∈ ({2, 3, 4, 6} : Finset ℕ) :=
  (quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints hO μ H b ι
    τ).trans (quotientMk_mem_shimuraAdelicEllipticPoints_iff_natCard_mem hO μ H b ι τ hB)

lemma completedUnitsToUnits_unitsToCompletedUnits (u : Oˣ) :
    O.completedUnitsToUnits (O.unitsToCompletedUnits u) =
      Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (O.unitsToNormalizer u : Bˣ) :=
  Units.ext (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebraFun_of_mem hO (u : O).2).symm

lemma completedUnitsToUnits_injective : Function.Injective O.completedUnitsToUnits := by
  intro x y h
  have h₁ : O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder x /ₒ (1 : O.completedOrderPosNat) =
      O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder y /ₒ 1 :=
    congrArg Units.val h
  rcases oreDiv_eq_iff.mp h₁ with ⟨⟨_, n, hn, rfl⟩, v, h₂, h₃⟩
  rw [Submonoid.smul_def, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul] at h₂
  have h₄ : (n : O.completedOrder) = v :=
    (mul_one _).symm.trans (h₃.trans (mul_one v))
  have h₅ : (n : O.completedOrder) * (O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder y -
      O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder x) = 0 := by
    rw [mul_sub, sub_eq_zero]
    exact h₂.trans (congrArg (· * _) h₄.symm)
  have h₆ : O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder y = O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder x :=
    sub_eq_zero.mp (O.eq_zero_of_natCast_mul_eq_zero (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero hn) h₅)
  exact Subtype.ext <| funext fun N ↦ Units.ext (congrFun (congrArg Subtype.val h₆) N).symm

variable (q : ℚˣ)

lemma map_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_comp_algebraMap :
    Units.map ((O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).comp (algebraMap ℚ B)).toMonoidHom q =
      Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B) q) :=
  rfl

lemma map_algebraMap_mem_unitsNormalizer :
    Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B) q ∈ O.unitsNormalizer := fun x ↦ by
  have hc : (↑(Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B) q) : B) * x =
      x * ↑(Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B) q) :=
    Algebra.commutes (q : ℚ) x
  rw [hc, Units.mul_inv_cancel_right]

/-- **The geometric component of `X_H` through the points `[τ, 1]` is ZF7's `Γ_H^+ \ ℍ`**: the
group `Γ_1 = B^×_+ ∩ K_H` is the group `Γ_H^+` of `Subalgebra.shimuraGammaPlus`, using
`B ∩ Ô = O`. -/
lemma shimuraAdelicGamma_one :
    shimuraAdelicGamma hO μ H 1 ι = (O.shimuraGammaPlus μ H ι).map O.unitsNormalizer.subtype := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun γ' hγ' ↦ ?_) (Subgroup.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun γ hγ ↦ ?_)
  · rcases Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hγ' with ⟨⟨⟨x, w, hw⟩, hH, hF⟩, hpos⟩
    rcases QuotientGroup.mk_surjective w with ⟨w', rfl⟩
    have hF' : (QuotientGroup.mk (O.completedUnitsToUnits x *
        Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (w' : Bˣ)) :
        O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ ⧸ finiteAdelicRatUnits hO) =
        QuotientGroup.mk (Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom γ') := by
      refine hF.trans ?_
      simp
    rcases QuotientGroup.eq.mp hF' with ⟨q, hq⟩
    rw [map_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_comp_algebraMap] at hq
    let v : Bˣ := γ' * (Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B) q)⁻¹ * (w' : Bˣ)⁻¹
    have hv : O.completedUnitsToUnits x = Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom v := by
      rw [map_mul, map_mul, map_inv, map_inv, hq]
      group
    have hv₁ : (v : B) ∈ O :=
      O.mem_of_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_mem hO <| O.mem_completedOrderSubalgebra_iff.mpr
        ⟨O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder x, congrArg Units.val hv⟩
    have hv₂ : (↑v⁻¹ : B) ∈ O :=
      O.mem_of_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_mem hO <| O.mem_completedOrderSubalgebra_iff.mpr
        ⟨O.completedUnitsToCompletedOrder x⁻¹,
          congrArg (fun z : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebraˣ ↦ (↑z⁻¹ : O.FiniteAdelicAlgebra)) hv⟩
    let u : Oˣ := ⟨⟨_, hv₁⟩, ⟨_, hv₂⟩, Subtype.ext (Units.mul_inv v), Subtype.ext (Units.inv_mul v)⟩
    have hx : x = O.unitsToCompletedUnits u :=
      completedUnitsToUnits_injective
        (hv.trans (completedUnitsToUnits_unitsToCompletedUnits hO u).symm)
    subst hx
    have hγ : ((O.unitsToNormalizer u * w' * ⟨_, map_algebraMap_mem_unitsNormalizer q⟩ :
        O.unitsNormalizer) : Bˣ) = γ' := by
      have h₁ : (O.unitsToNormalizer u : Bˣ) =
          γ' * (Units.map (algebraMap ℚ B : ℚ →* B) q)⁻¹ * (w' : Bˣ)⁻¹ :=
        Units.ext rfl
      rw [Subgroup.coe_mul, Subgroup.coe_mul, h₁, Subgroup.coe_mk]
      group
    refine ⟨O.unitsToNormalizer u * w' * ⟨_, map_algebraMap_mem_unitsNormalizer q⟩,
      Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨⟨⟨u, ⟨_, hw⟩⟩, hH, QuotientGroup.eq.mpr ⟨q, ?_⟩⟩, ?_⟩, hγ⟩
    · simp only [Subgroup.coe_subtype]
      group
    · rw [Subgroup.mem_comap, normalizerToGL, MonoidHom.comp_apply, Subgroup.coe_subtype, hγ]
      exact hpos
  · rcases Subgroup.mem_inf.mp hγ with ⟨⟨⟨u, w, hw⟩, hy, hyγ⟩, hpos⟩
    rcases QuotientGroup.mk_surjective w with ⟨w', rfl⟩
    have h₂ : (QuotientGroup.mk (O.unitsToNormalizer u * w') : O.NormalizerModScalars) =
        QuotientGroup.mk γ :=
      hyγ
    rcases QuotientGroup.eq.mp h₂ with ⟨q, hq⟩
    refine Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨⟨O.enhancedGroupOfUnits μ ⟨u, ⟨_, hw⟩⟩, hy, ?_⟩, hpos⟩
    have hF : enhancedGroupToFiniteAdelic hO μ (O.enhancedGroupOfUnits μ ⟨u, ⟨_, hw⟩⟩) =
        QuotientGroup.mk (O.completedUnitsToUnits (O.unitsToCompletedUnits u) *
          Units.map (O.toFiniteAdelicAlgebra hO).toMonoidHom (w' : Bˣ)) :=
      rfl
    rw [hF, completedUnitsToUnits_unitsToCompletedUnits hO, ← map_mul]
    refine QuotientGroup.eq.mpr ⟨q, ?_⟩
    refine (map_toFiniteAdelicAlgebra_comp_algebraMap hO q).trans ?_
    simp only [hq, MonoidHom.comp_apply, MulEquiv.coe_toMonoidHom, MulAut.conj_apply, inv_one,
      one_mul, mul_one, Subgroup.coe_subtype, map_mul, map_inv]

/-- **The elliptic points of `X_H` on the geometric component through the points `[τ, 1]` are those
of ZF7** (`Subalgebra.shimuraEllipticPoints`): `[τ, 1]` is an elliptic point of `X_H` exactly when
the orbit of `τ` under `Γ_H^+` is an elliptic point of `Γ_H^+ \ ℍ`. -/
lemma quotientMk_one_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff :
    (Quotient.mk _ (τ, 1) : ShimuraCurvePoints hO μ H ι) ∈ shimuraCurveEllipticPoints hO μ H ι ↔
    (Quotient.mk _ τ : orbitRel.Quotient (O.shimuraGammaPlus μ H ι) ℍ) ∈
      O.shimuraEllipticPoints μ H ι := by
  rw [quotientMk_mem_shimuraCurveEllipticPoints_iff, shimuraAdelicGamma_one,
    quotientMk_mem_shimuraEllipticPoints_iff]
  exact ⟨fun ⟨_, ⟨γ, hγ, rfl⟩, hγτ, hγQ⟩ ↦
    ⟨⟨γ, hγ⟩, hγτ, fun h ↦ hγQ (Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mp h)⟩,
    fun ⟨γ, hγτ, hγQ⟩ ↦ ⟨_, ⟨γ, γ.2, rfl⟩, hγτ, fun h ↦ hγQ (Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.mpr h)⟩⟩

end Subalgebra
